Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:33:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Test transfer-impedance interface layers against physics
 and the wire
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The core tests pinned the block and the jump. These pin what the layer
must do as physics and through every path a request can take.

- Voltage-driven transducer: monolithic equals condensed :none (retained
  and condensed transducer) and :pressure to 1e-9.
- Positive- and negative-time solves with a mass term are conjugates,
  monolithic and condensed.
- Power: with a lossless interior, piston power = layer + radiated, and
  the layer dissipates R/2 ∫|v|^2, consistent and nodal, to 1e-9.
- Lumped Helmholtz resonator on the coupled fixture: vent flow within
  1 % and 0.5 degrees of the series-impedance prediction at <= 100 Hz; a
  mass layer sized to lower f_H by 30 % lowers it by 30 % within 2 %.
- FP32 with R up to 10^6 rho c: flux and interior hold 1e-4 on every
  path; the exterior pressure of the unreduced layout degrades ~10x per
  decade above 10 rho c (cancellation in p_F - p_B), :pressure and Float64
  refinement do not. Recorded, not clamped.
- CUDA and ROCm device paths against CPU, gated on hardware; they skip as
  broken tests with a warning.
- contract_tests.jl loads coupled_solver.jl into its own module and drives
  solve_request: the layer is parsed and reported with the convention's
  sign, every malformed or misplaced layer is refused with its message,
  and the speaker ROM refuses a layered system.

